            {
              "cardId": "c_1064_eps",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Kayron's gimmick is that he creates Futility Cards and needs to Exhaust them\nFutility cards at a base are a 1 AP, Exhaustible \"Status Ailment\" Card\nHis whole goal is to create as many Futility as he can, and exhaust them\nBria and Kayron E3 are very efficent ways to completely clear Futilities\nUse Bria/Kayron E3 right before you reshuffle for the most Value\nThey are both a very big spike for Kayron"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Oath of Vanity"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1064_uni3",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1064_uni3",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Kayron's MOST Important card, changes his playstyle\nKayron's Futilities are only Status cards before Oath\nUsing them as Status is very inefficent, but if you don't it clogs your deck\nOath can change Futilities into Attack cards to do damage and/or heal also\nOath 4 is the truely Kayron play style defining epiphany\nOath 4 lets you easily fill your hands of Futilities then instantly Exhaust many\nBut since it has exhaust itself, and doesn't change Futilities into Attacks\nIf you can't win that early, you need either Bria or Kayron E3 to start making sure\nThat Futilities will not clog your deck"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1064_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1064_uni2",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1064_tut1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Multiplicative synergy and Allies Exhaust"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Kayron is a little special, and his scaling damage on Echo and Black Hole\nAre affected by Multiplicative Damage Sources, so Void Set and Equipment\nKayron usually only cares about exhausting his own Futility, but Brand\nBrand 0,1,2,4 are versions that can also care about how many cards are\nExhausted by his Allies"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
